                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-03",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "general airway management should be initiated to ensure the child's airway is open and stable. This may include oxygen therapy, positioning, and possibly intubation or tracheostomy if necessary. \n\nAfter airway management, the recommended treatment for this presentation is nebulized racemic epinephrine. This can help reduce airway inflammation and improve breathing. Corticosteroids may also be given to further reduce inflammation. Antibiotics may be considered if there is suspicion of a bacterial infection, but they are not the first-line treatment for this presentation. Anti-diphtheria toxin would only be given if the child is confirmed to have diphtheria, which is rare in most countries due to vaccination programs.",
