                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe symptoms described suggest a possible case of acute epiglottitis, which is a medical emergency. The first step in management is to secure the airway, which is the general airway management mentioned in the question stem. Once the airway is secured, the next step is to administer antibiotics to treat the underlying infection. Therefore, option D, IV ceftriaxone, is the recommended treatment in addition to general airway management. Options A and C may be used as adjunctive therapy, but they are not the primary treatment for acute epiglottitis. Option B is not relevant in this case as diphtheria is a rare cause of acute epiglottitis in developed countries.",
