                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " The patient has an altered sensorium, which means they are not oriented and may be confused. The first thing you want to do is make sure they are not hypoglycemic or hyperglycemic, so you would check their blood sugar. Then you want to make sure there is no bleeding in the brain, so you would do a non-contrast CT head. Then you want to make sure there is no infection in the brain, so you would do a lumbar puncture. Finally, you want to make sure there is no underlying medical condition causing the altered sensorium, so you would do a complete blood count.",
