                        "cot": " Before supplementing calcium to a neonate, it is important to know the underlying cause of the low calcium level. Therefore, the first step would be to check the blood glucose level to rule out hypoglycemia as a cause. After that, it is important to check the serum protein and bilirubin levels to rule out any liver or kidney diseases that could be causing the low calcium level. Finally, it is important to check the oxygen saturation level to ensure that the neonate is receiving adequate oxygenation.",
