                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nA) Blood glucose: It is important to know the blood glucose level before supplementing calcium to a neonate because if the blood glucose level is low, calcium supplementation may cause hypoglycemia.\n\nB) Serum protein: It is important to know the serum protein level before supplementing calcium to a neonate because if the serum protein level is low, calcium supplementation may cause hypoalbuminemia.\n\nC) Serum bilirubin: It is important to know the serum bilirubin level before supplementing calcium to a neonate because if the serum bilirubin level is high, calcium supplementation may cause hyperbilirubinemia.\n\nD) Oxygen saturation: It is important to know the oxygen saturation level before supplementing calcium to a neonate because if the oxygen saturation level is low, calcium supplementation may cause hypoxemia.",
