                        "cot": "Before supplementing calcium to a neonate with a serum calcium level of 6 mg/dL, it is important to know the serum protein levels (option B). This is because calcium binds to albumin, a protein in the blood, and the total serum calcium level includes both bound and unbound (free) calcium. In cases of low serum protein levels, the total serum calcium may appear low, even if the free calcium levels are normal. Therefore, it is essential to know the serum protein levels to accurately assess the neonate's calcium status and determine the appropriate supplementation.",
