                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's think step by step about how the condyle moves laterally. The first thing that needs to happen is that the articular disc needs to be displaced. This is done by the action of the lateral pterygoid muscle. The next thing that needs to happen is that the condyle needs to be rotated. This is done by the action of the medial pterygoid muscle.",
