                    {
                        "id": "1869a50c-d67f-47e3-9c7d-cdd2890465b4",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's understand what each term means:\n\n- Lateral movement: Movement to the side (left or right)\n- Condyle: The rounded end of a bone that articulates with another bone (in this case, the mandibular condyle, which is part of the temporomandibular joint)\n- Contralateral: On the opposite side of the body\n- Ipsilateral: On the same side of the body\n- Lateral pterygoid: A muscle involved in jaw movement\n- Medial pterygoid: Another muscle involved in jaw movement\n\nNow, let's consider the role of each muscle in jaw movement:\n\n- The lateral pterygoid muscle has two heads (superior and inferior) and is responsible for protrusion (forward movement) and lateral movement of the mandible.\n- The medial pterygoid muscle works together with the masseter muscle to elevate the mandible (close the jaw).\n\nConsidering these roles, we can eliminate option C (same side medial pterygoid) as it is not involved in lateral movement.\n\nNow, let's think about the lateral pterygoid muscle and its involvement in lateral movement. When the mandible moves laterally, it is moving to one side. For example, if the mandible moves to the right, the right condyle is moving forward and the left condyle is moving backward. This movement is caused by the contraction of the ipsilateral (same side) lateral pterygoid muscle. In this example, the right lateral pterygoid muscle would contract to move the mandible to the right.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n\nB) Ipsilateral lateral pterygoid",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "105a2ea2-8eed-472b-90d3-f2364252c687",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) Ipsilateral lateral pterygoid",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
