                        "cot": "A child with a debranching enzyme deficiency has a low blood glucose level. Intravenous glucagon given after meals raises the blood glucose levels, but does not raise glucose when given after an overnight fast. Liver biopsy shows increased glycogen in liver. The enzyme likely to be defective in this child is D-branching enzyme. So, the answer is D.",
