                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we need to understand what each rule refers to:\n\nA) McNaughton's rule: a rule used to determine the direction of a bullet wound based on the shape of the entrance and exit wounds.\n\nB) Puppe's rule: a rule used to determine the age of a fetus based on the length of its femur bone.\n\nC) Young's rule: a rule used to calculate pediatric doses of medication based on the child's age and weight.\n\nD) Dunlop's rule: a rule used to determine the sequence of fractures in the skull based on the location and direction of the fractures.\n\nSince we are dealing with fractures in the skull, the correct answer is D) Dunlop's rule.",
