                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe correct answer is B) Puppe's rule.\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- An autopsy was performed on a case of accidental death.\n- It showed two linear fractures on petrous pa of temporal bone.\n- Linear fractures are fractures that occur in a straight line.\n- The petrous part of the temporal bone is a pyramid-shaped bone located at the base of the skull, between the sphenoid and occipital bones.\n- Therefore, the fractures occurred in the petrous part of the temporal bone.\n- The question asks for the rule that gives the sequence of fractures.\n- McNaughton's rule is a rule used to determine the direction of a bullet wound, not the sequence of fractures.\n- Young's rule is a rule used to calculate drug dosages based on the patient's age and weight, not related to fractures.\n- Dunlop's rule is a rule used to determine the direction of a fracture line, not the sequence of fractures.\n- Puppe's rule is a rule used to determine the sequence of fractures in the petrous part of the temporal bone.\n- Therefore, the correct answer is B) Puppe's rule.",
