                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "it should be noted that the correct spelling is \"Q test\" (without the apostrophe). \n\nThe answer is B) To determine outliers. \n\nThe Q test is a statistical test used to identify outliers in a dataset. It is based on the assumption that in a normal distribution, the gap between adjacent values should be roughly the same. The Q test calculates the ratio of the gap between the outlier and its nearest neighbor to the range of the entire dataset. If this ratio exceeds a certain critical value, the outlier is considered significant and can be removed from the dataset. \n\nThe Q test is not used for comparing means or proportions of groups, nor is it used to determine normality distribution.",
