                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nGrey communicans are part of the autonomic nervous system and connect spinal nerves to sympathetic ganglia. They are responsible for transmitting preganglionic fibers from the spinal cord to the ganglia. Therefore, options B and C are true.\n\nGrey communicans are unmyelinated, which means they lack a myelin sheath. This is important because myelin sheaths increase the speed of nerve impulses. Therefore, option A is also true.\n\nThe white ramus communicans is a myelinated nerve fiber that connects spinal nerves to sympathetic ganglia. The grey communicans, on the other hand, are unmyelinated and present medial to the white ramus communicans. Therefore, option D is false.\n\nThe correct answer is D) Present medial to the white ramus communicans.",
