                        "cot": " Metformin is a medication used to treat type 2 diabetes. It works by decreasing the amount of sugar produced by the liver and absorbed by the intestines. Lactic acidosis is a serious side effect of metformin, and it occurs when there is too much lactic acid in the blood. Factors that increase the risk of lactic acidosis include advanced age, liver dysfunction, renal failure, and alcohol consumption. The correct answer is B) Smoking.",
