                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Identify the location of the lesion\nThe enhancing mass is seen in the nasopharynx with minimal extension into the sphenoid sinus and no lateral extension.\n\nStep 2: Determine the T stage based on the location and size of the lesion\nAccording to the American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) staging system for nasopharyngeal cancer, T stage is determined based on the size and location of the primary tumor. \n\nT1: Tumor confined to the nasopharynx\nT2: Tumor extends to the oropharynx and/or nasal cavity\nT3: Tumor invades bony structures and/or paranasal sinuses\nT4: Tumor invades the cranial nerves, hypopharynx, orbit, or other adjacent structures\n\nBased on the location of the lesion, it is confined to the nasopharynx, which corresponds to T1.\n\nStep 3: Determine the N stage based on the involvement of regional lymph nodes\nThe N stage is determined based on the involvement of regional lymph nodes.\n\nN0: No regional lymph node metastasis\nN1: Unilateral metastasis in lymph node(s) \u22646 cm in greatest dimension\nN2: Bilateral metastasis in lymph node(s) \u22646 cm in greatest dimension or unilateral metastasis in lymph node(s) >6 cm but \u2264 12 cm in greatest dimension\nN3: Metastasis in lymph node(s) >12 cm in greatest dimension or metastasis in a lymph node(s) along the spinal accessory nerve\n\nThere is no information provided about the involvement of regional lymph nodes, so we cannot determine the N stage.\n\nStep 4: Determine the overall stage based on T and N stages\nAccording to the AJCC staging system, the overall stage is determined based on the T and N stages.\n\nStage I: T1, N0\nStage II: T2, N0 or T1-2, N1\nStage III: T3, N0-1 or T1-3, N2\nStage IV: T4, any N or any T, N3\n\nBased on the T stage, the overall stage is IA.\n\nTherefore, the answer is A) IA.",
                        "answers": [
