                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nA) Safety: The main aim of Phase 1 clinical trials is to assess the safety of a new drug or treatment. This includes determining the side effects, dosage, and safety profile of the drug or treatment.\n\nB) Efficacy: While efficacy is an important factor to consider, it is not the main aim of Phase 1 clinical trials.\n\nC) Dose: Dose is an important factor to consider in Phase 1 clinical trials, as it helps to determine the safety and efficacy of the drug or treatment.\n\nD) Pharmacokinetics: Pharmacokinetics is an important factor to consider in Phase 1 clinical trials, as it helps to determine the absorption, distribution, metabolism, and excretion of the drug or treatment.",
