                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The main aim of phase 1 clinical trials is to determine the maximum tolerated dose (MTD) of a new drug. This is the dose at which side effects are seen in a significant number of people, but which is not so high as to be immediately life-threatening. Phase 1 trials are usually conducted with a small number of healthy volunteers, and the MTD is determined by gradually increasing the dose and observing the effects.\nThe main aim of phase 1 clinical trials is to determine the maximum tolerated dose (MTD) of a new drug. This is the dose at which side effects are seen in a significant number of people, but which is not so high as to be immediately life-threatening. Phase 1 trials are usually conducted with a small number of healthy volunteers, and the MTD is determined by gradually increasing the dose and observing the effects.",
