                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nPhase 1 clinical trials are the first stage of testing a new drug or treatment in humans. The primary goal of phase 1 clinical trials is to evaluate the safety of the drug or treatment. Therefore, the correct answer is A) Safety. \n\nWhile efficacy, dose, and pharmacokinetics are important factors to consider in clinical trials, they are typically evaluated in later phases of clinical development. In phase 1, the focus is on determining the safety profile of the drug or treatment, including any potential side effects or adverse reactions. Once safety has been established, researchers can move on to evaluating efficacy, optimal dosing, and other factors.",
