                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe major aim of phase 1 clinical trials is safety. \n\nPhase 1 clinical trials are the first stage of testing a new drug or treatment in humans. These trials are usually conducted on a small group of healthy volunteers to evaluate the safety and tolerability of the drug. \n\nDuring phase 1 trials, researchers monitor the participants closely for any adverse effects or side effects of the drug. They also study the pharmacokinetics of the drug, which refers to how the drug is absorbed, distributed, metabolized, and eliminated by the body. \n\nWhile efficacy and dose are important considerations in drug development, they are not the primary focus of phase 1 trials. The main goal of phase 1 trials is to determine the safety of the drug and to establish a safe dosage range for further testing in later phases of clinical trials. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) Safety.",
