                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": " A) Diffuse axonal injury.\n\nDiffuse axonal injury is a type of traumatic brain injury that occurs when the brain is shaken or rotated rapidly, causing the nerve fibers in the brain to stretch and tear. This type of injury is often seen in cases of falls, car accidents, and other traumatic events. Retrograde amnesia, or the inability to remember events that occurred before the injury, is a common symptom of diffuse axonal injury.",
