                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-09",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe Krebs cycle involves the conversion of Acetyl-CoA to produce energy in the form of ATP. Acetyl-CoA is formed from the breakdown of pyruvate, which is derived from glucose metabolism. Therefore, amino acids that can be converted to pyruvate can enter the Krebs cycle by forming Acetyl-CoA.\n\nGlycine, Alanine, and Hydroxyproline can all be converted to pyruvate through various metabolic pathways. However, Tyrosine cannot be directly converted to pyruvate.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) Tyrosine.",
