                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nThe Golgi tendon organ is a type of proprioceptor. Proprioceptors are sensors that detect changes in the position or tension of muscles and tendons. \n\nThe Golgi tendon organ is located at the junction of a muscle and tendon. It is stimulated by changes in muscle tension. When the muscle contracts, the tendon is pulled. This stretches the Golgi tendon organ, which sends a signal to the spinal cord that the muscle is contracting. \n\nThe Golgi tendon organ is used to detect changes in muscle tension. It is not used to detect static muscle length, dynamic muscle length, or muscle action.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "0dd149b2-3ca1-45f2-805d-ef694a852e32",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
