                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's think step by step about what would happen in this case. \n\nThe IOL would be placed in the young male's eye, and after 10 years, the IOL should be removed in case of posterior capsular ossification. This is because the IOL can cause the posterior capsular to ossify, and over time, this can lead to decreased vision.",
