                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understanding the lymph node structure\nBefore answering the question, it is important to understand the structure of a lymph node. A lymph node is an oval-shaped organ that is part of the lymphatic system. It is composed of an outer capsule, a cortex, and a medulla. The cortex is the outer layer of the lymph node, and it contains lymphatic nodules and cords of cells called the cords of Billroth. The medulla is the inner layer of the lymph node, and it contains sinuses and medullary cords.\n\nStep 2: Eliminating options\nThe question asks which of the given options is present in the cortex of the lymph node. Therefore, we can eliminate option D, which refers to the white pulp. The white pulp is a component of the spleen, not the lymph node.\n\nStep 3: Understanding the options\nOption A, cords of Billroth, are a network of cells that support the lymphatic nodules in the cortex of the lymph node. Option B, Hassall's corpuscles, are structures found in the thymus gland, not the lymph node. Option C, lymphatic nodules, are small, spherical structures found in the cortex of the lymph node. They are composed of lymphocytes and are involved in the immune response.\n\nStep 4: Answering the question\nBased on the above information, the correct answer to the question is option C, lymphatic nodules. The cortex of the lymph node contains lymphatic nodules and cords of cells called the cords of Billroth. Therefore, option A is also partially correct, but option C is a more specific answer to the question.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "a9ac597f-affd-4d35-ae4f-9d56c5498fea",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) Lymphatic nodules.",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
