                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe correct answer is B) First pass effect.\n\nHere's why:\n\nExcretion refers to the removal of a drug from the body after it has been metabolized and circulated through the bloodstream. This process typically occurs in the kidneys and liver.\n\nFirst order elimination refers to the rate at which a drug is eliminated from the body, which is typically proportional to the concentration of the drug in the bloodstream. This process is influenced by factors such as the drug's half-life and the efficiency of the body's elimination mechanisms.\n\nMetabolism refers to the process by which a drug is broken down into its component parts by enzymes in the body. This process can occur in various organs, including the liver, kidneys, and intestines.\n\nThe first pass effect, on the other hand, refers specifically to the process by which a drug is metabolized and eliminated by the liver before it enters the systemic circulation. This occurs because drugs that are taken orally are absorbed into the bloodstream through the digestive system, which sends them directly to the liver via the hepatic portal vein. The liver then metabolizes the drug before it can reach other parts of the body, which can reduce the drug's effectiveness and alter its pharmacokinetic properties.",
