                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand Piaget's stages of cognitive development\nPiaget's theory of cognitive development suggests that children go through four stages of cognitive development: sensorimotor, preoperational, concrete operational, and formal operational. The preoperational stage is the second stage and occurs between the ages of 2 and 7.\n\nStep 2: Identify the options\nA) Birth to 18 months\nB) 12 years onwards.\nC) 2-6 years.\nD) 7-12 years.\n\nStep 3: Eliminate the options\nOption A is incorrect because it refers to the sensorimotor stage, which occurs from birth to 2 years. Option B is incorrect because it refers to the formal operational stage, which occurs from 12 years onwards. Option D is incorrect because it refers to the concrete operational stage, which occurs from 7 to 12 years.\n\nStep 4: Choose the correct option\nOption C is correct because it refers to the preoperational stage, which occurs from 2 to 6 years.\n\nTherefore, the answer is C) 2-6 years.",
