                        "cot": "\n\nThe correct answer is C) 2-6 years.\n\nPiaget's theory of cognitive development suggests that children go through four stages of cognitive development: sensorimotor, preoperational, concrete operational, and formal operational. The preoperational stage is the second stage and occurs between the ages of 2 and 6 years.\n\nDuring this stage, children develop symbolic thinking, which allows them to use words and images to represent objects and ideas. They also begin to understand the concept of conservation, which means that the amount of a substance remains the same even if its appearance changes.\n\nTherefore, option C) 2-6 years is the correct answer.",
