                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking about the method used to evaluate post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB.\n\nStep 2: Understand the options\nA) Active surveillance: This involves actively seeking out cases of a particular disease or condition.\nB) Sentinel surveillance: This involves monitoring a specific group of people or location for early detection of a disease or condition.\nC) Passive surveillance: This involves relying on healthcare providers to report cases of a disease or condition.\nD) Routine checkup of all operated cases: This involves regularly checking on all patients who have undergone cataract extraction surgery under PCB.\n\nStep 3: Determine the correct answer\nThe best option for evaluating post-operative vision effects after cataract extraction surgery under PCB would be routine checkup of all operated cases (option D). This would involve regularly checking on all patients who have undergone the surgery to monitor their vision and detect any potential complications.\n\nOption A (active surveillance) and option B (sentinel surveillance) are not appropriate for this situation as they involve monitoring for the occurrence of a disease or condition, rather than evaluating the effects of a specific surgery.\n\nOption C (passive surveillance) may be used to monitor complications or adverse events related to the surgery, but it would not be the best option for evaluating post-operative vision effects.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) Routine checkup of all operated cases.",
