                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nX-Linked SCID is a severe combined immunodeficiency disorder caused by mutations in the IL2RG gene, which encodes for the common gamma chain (\u03b3c) of several cytokine receptors, including the interleukin-2 (IL-2) receptor. Therefore, the correct answer is D) IL2RG. \n\nEGFR (epidermal growth factor receptor) is not directly related to X-Linked SCID, although it may play a role in some types of cancer. CD23 (cluster of differentiation 23) is a protein involved in B-cell activation and differentiation, but it is not associated with X-Linked SCID. IL6 (interleukin-6) is a cytokine that regulates inflammation and immune responses, but it is not directly involved in X-Linked SCID either.",
                        "answers": [
