                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "it is important to note that the reverse bevel incision is a type of incision used in periodontal surgery. The correct answer is D) All of the above. \n\nThe reverse bevel incision is designed to provide access to the alveolar crest, remove infected tissue in the sulcus, and allow atraumatic reflection of the gingival margin. The incision is made on the lingual or palatal surface of the tooth, and the bevel is directed towards the tooth. This allows for a more precise incision and better access to the affected area. The reverse bevel incision is commonly used in procedures such as crown lengthening, pocket reduction, and osseous surgery.",
                        "answers": [
