                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " Intracellular killing of microbes requires that the microbe be inside of a cell, right? So we need a mechanism by which a microbe can enter a cell.\n\nOne way that a microbe can enter a cell is by phagocytosis, which is a process by which a cell engulfs and then breaks down a foreign particle. Phagocytosis is mediated by inflammatory mediators such as cytokines and chemokines.\n\nOnce the microbe is inside the cell, it needs to be killed. This is where lysozyme comes in. Lysozyme is an enzyme that breaks down the cell wall of bacteria.\n\nSo the answer is C) Lysozyme",
                        "answers": [
