                    {
                        "id": "97d223c0-93ff-48c6-8cd4-3492c596b22b_0",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's think step by step about how to calculate this. \n\nFirst, we need to calculate the change in volume. The tidal volume is the volume of air inhaled or exhaled in a single breath. In this case, the patient inhaled 500 mL of air. This is the change in volume.\n\nNext, we need to calculate the change in pressure. The intrapleural pressure was measured as -4 cm of water before inspiration and -9 cm of water after inspiration. This is the change in pressure.\n\nNow we can calculate the compliance. Compliance is the change in volume divided by the change in pressure. In this case, the compliance would be 500 mL/-5 cm H\u2082O, or 0.1 L/cm.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "0",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "0.1 L/cm",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "lievin",
                        "date": null,
                        "api_service": "",
                        "model": "{'name': 'text-davinci-002'}",
                        "comment": "",
                        "annotations": []
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "97d223c0-93ff-48c6-8cd4-3492c596b22b_1",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "lievin-10",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Let's think step by step like a medical expert.\n\nFirst, what is the definition of pulmonary compliance? It is the amount of lung expansion per unit of increase in pressure. In other words, it is a measure of how \"stretchy\" the lungs are.\n\nSecond, what is the formula for pulmonary compliance? It is the tidal volume divided by the difference in intrapleural pressure.\n\nIn this case, the tidal volume is 500 mL and the difference in intrapleural pressure is 9 cm of water - 4 cm of water, or 5 cm of water. Therefore, the pulmonary compliance in this patient is 500 mL divided by 5 cm of water, or 0.1 L/cm.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "0",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "0.1 L/cm",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "lievin",
                        "date": null,
