                    {
                        "id": "b5769165-fca9-48a5-bd88-e27927f956ca",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe formula for pulmonary compliance is:\n\nCompliance = change in volume / change in pressure\n\nThe change in volume is the tidal volume, which is 500 mL. The change in pressure is the difference between the intrapleural pressure before and after inspiration, which is:\n\n-9 cmH2O - (-4 cmH2O) = -5 cmH2O\n\nHowever, we need to convert this pressure difference to units of liters, since the tidal volume is in liters. 1 cmH2O is equivalent to 0.098 kPa, and 1 liter is equivalent to 1000 mL, so:\n\n-5 cmH2O x 0.098 kPa/cmH2O x 1 L/1000 mL = -0.0049 L\n\nNow we can calculate the compliance:\n\nCompliance = 500 mL / (-0.0049 L) = -102.04 mL/cmH2O\n\nHowever, the answer choices are in units of L/cm, so we need to convert:\n\n-102.04 mL/cmH2O x 1 L/1000 mL = -0.102 L/cmH2O\n\nSince compliance is a positive value, we can take the absolute value:\n\nCompliance = 0.102 L/cmH2O\n\nTherefore, the answer is C) 0.2 L/cm.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "6bb3992a-c902-433b-af51-7cb619f7159b",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) 0.2 L/cm.",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/03/11 01:37:42",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
                        "model": "{'name': 'gpt-3.5-turbo', 'temperature': 0, 'max_tokens': 512}",
                        "comment": "",
                        "annotations": []
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "9be9fc21-3887-43a1-bac1-b2bb8b5ce23c",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we need to calculate the change in intrapleural pressure during inspiration:\n\n\u0394P = Pfinal - Pinitial\n\u0394P = (-9 cmH2O) - (-4 cmH2O)\n\u0394P = -5 cmH2O\n\nNext, we can use the formula for pulmonary compliance:\n\nC = \u0394V / \u0394P\n\nwhere \u0394V is the change in volume and \u0394P is the change in pressure.\n\nWe know that the tidal volume is 500 mL, so \u0394V = 0.5 L. Plugging in the values we have:\n\nC = 0.5 L / (-5 cmH2O)\nC = -0.1 L/cmH2O\n\nNote that the units of pressure are different from the units of volume, so we need to convert cmH2O to L/cmH2O:\n\n1 cmH2O = 0.098 kPa\n1 L = 1000 mL\n\nTherefore:\n\nC = -0.1 L / (-5 cmH2O) * (0.098 kPa/cmH2O) * (1000 mL/L)\nC = 0.2 L/cm\n\nSo the answer is C) 0.2 L/cm.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "e7dea3f5-0f7d-4a47-ad71-637f31354fba",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) 0.2 L/cm.",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/03/11 01:37:56",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
                        "model": "{'name': 'gpt-3.5-turbo', 'temperature': 0, 'max_tokens': 512}",
                        "comment": "",
                        "annotations": []
                    },
                    {
                        "id": "5357a805-6628-4d87-b035-65a7cf1b987b",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we need to calculate the change in intrapleural pressure during inspiration:\n\nChange in intrapleural pressure = final intrapleural pressure - initial intrapleural pressure\n= (-9 cmH2O) - (-4 cmH2O)\n= -5 cmH2O\n\nNext, we need to calculate the transpulmonary pressure, which is the difference between the alveolar pressure and the intrapleural pressure:\n\nTranspulmonary pressure = alveolar pressure - intrapleural pressure\n\nSince the alveolar pressure is atmospheric pressure (0 cmH2O) during inspiration, we can simplify this to:\n\nTranspulmonary pressure = 0 cmH2O - (-9 cmH2O)\n= 9 cmH2O\n\nFinally, we can calculate the pulmonary compliance using the formula:\n\nPulmonary compliance = tidal volume / transpulmonary pressure\n\nPlugging in the values we have:\n\nPulmonary compliance = 500 mL / 9 cmH2O\n= 55.6 mL/cmH2O\n= 0.056 L/cmH2O\n\nRounding to one decimal place, the answer is:\n\nC) 0.2 L/cm",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "ce135073-e845-4ae0-9e25-f50ccc555188",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) 0.2 L/cm.",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
