                    {
                        "id": "e2305a6e-104b-4953-b0c7-6e7a67a00e78",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-01",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nPulmonary compliance is defined as the change in lung volume per unit change in transpulmonary pressure. \n\nThe transpulmonary pressure is the difference between the alveolar pressure and the intrapleural pressure. \n\nTherefore, the change in transpulmonary pressure during inspiration can be calculated as follows: \n\nChange in transpulmonary pressure = alveolar pressure - intrapleural pressure \n\nBefore inspiration: \nAlveolar pressure = atmospheric pressure = 0 cm of water \nIntrapleural pressure = -4 cm of water \n\nTranspulmonary pressure before inspiration = 0 - (-4) = 4 cm of water \n\nAfter inspiration: \nAlveolar pressure = atmospheric pressure = 0 cm of water \nIntrapleural pressure = -9 cm of water \n\nTranspulmonary pressure after inspiration = 0 - (-9) = 9 cm of water \n\nThe change in transpulmonary pressure during inspiration = 9 - 4 = 5 cm of water \n\nThe tidal volume is given as 500 mL. \n\nTherefore, pulmonary compliance can be calculated as follows: \n\nPulmonary compliance = tidal volume / change in transpulmonary pressure \n\nPulmonary compliance = 500 mL / 5 cm of water = 100 mL/cm of water \n\nSince 1 L = 1000 mL and 1 cm of water = 0.098 kPa, \n\nPulmonary compliance = 100 mL/cm of water = 0.1 L/kPa \n\nTherefore, the answer is A) 0.1 L/cm.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "30bf2805-348b-40e0-b441-085fd3d34e47",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "A) 0.1 L/cm.",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
                        "author": "thoughtsource",
                        "date": "2023/03/14 16:19:45",
                        "api_service": "openai_chat",
