                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nPulmonary compliance is defined as the change in lung volume per unit change in transpulmonary pressure. In this case, the change in lung volume is the tidal volume of 500 mL, and the change in transpulmonary pressure is the difference between the intrapleural pressure before and after inspiration, which is 5 cm of water (from -4 to -9 cm of water).\n\nTherefore, pulmonary compliance = tidal volume / change in transpulmonary pressure\n= 500 mL / 5 cmH2O\n= 100 mL/cmH2O\n= 0.1 L/cm\n\nSo the correct answer is A) 0.1 L/cm.",
