                        "cot": "Let's think step by step. The examiner is placing one hand under the patient's heel, which means the patient's foot is dorsiflexed. The patient is then asked to raise his other leg against downward resistance. This means the patient is trying to plantarflex his foot. The name of this test is the O'Donoghue test.",
