                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nC) Check for response and call help.\n\nThe first thing to do when presented with an unresponsive patient is to check for response and call for help. This is because the patient may be experiencing a medical emergency that requires immediate attention from medical professionals. \n\nTo check for response, gently tap the patient's shoulder and ask if they are okay. If there is no response, try to stimulate the patient by rubbing their sternum or pinching their earlobe. If there is still no response, call for help immediately. \n\nOnce help has been called, follow any instructions given by the emergency services operator. They may advise you to start chest compressions or rescue breaths, but it is important to wait for their guidance before taking any further action.",
                        "answers": [
