                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nOption A is true, as the optimum temperature for toxin production by Staphylococcus is 37\u00b0C.\n\nOption B is false, as Staphylococcus food poisoning is caused by the ingestion of preformed enterotoxins produced by the bacteria in contaminated food. These toxins are heat-stable and resistant to digestion, and they act on the gastrointestinal tract to cause symptoms such as nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea.\n\nOption C is false, as the enterotoxins produced by Staphylococcus are heat-stable and cannot be destroyed by boiling for 30 minutes.\n\nOption D is true, as the incubation period for Staphylococcus food poisoning is typically 1-6 hours after ingestion of contaminated food. \n\nTherefore, the characteristic feature of Staphylococcus food poisoning that is not true is option B.",
