                        "cot": "\n\nAnti-centromere antibodies are autoantibodies that target the centromere, a region of the chromosome that plays a crucial role in cell division. These antibodies are associated with certain autoimmune diseases, particularly scleroderma.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) Scleroderma.",
