                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " We are looking for a condition in which anti-centromere antibodies are seen. \n\nA) Drug-induced lupus: This is a condition in which the immune system attacks the body's own tissues and organs. Drug-induced lupus can be caused by certain medications, such as quinidine, procainamide, hydralazine, and isoniazid.\n\nB) SLE: This is a condition in which the immune system attacks the body's own tissues and organs. SLE can be caused by a variety of factors, including genetics, infections, and medications.\n\nC) Sjogren syndrome: This is a condition in which the immune system attacks the body's own tissues and organs. Sjogren syndrome can be caused by a variety of factors, including genetics, infections, and medications.\n\nD) Scleroderma: This is a condition in which the immune system attacks the body's own tissues and organs. Scleroderma can be caused by a variety of factors, including genetics, infections, and medications.",
                        "answers": [
