                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) Drug-induced lupus: This condition is characterized by the presence of anti-histone antibodies, not anti-centromere antibodies.\n\nB) SLE (Systemic Lupus Erythematosus): This condition is characterized by the presence of various autoantibodies, including anti-dsDNA, anti-Smith, and anti-phospholipid antibodies, but not anti-centromere antibodies.\n\nC) Sjogren syndrome: This condition is characterized by the presence of anti-Ro/SSA and anti-La/SSB antibodies, not anti-centromere antibodies.\n\nD) Scleroderma: This condition, also known as systemic sclerosis, is characterized by the presence of anti-centromere antibodies, particularly in the limited cutaneous form of the disease.\n\nBased on this information, the correct answer is:\n\nD) Scleroderma",
