                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) Squatting. \n\nSquatting helps to increase systemic vascular resistance and decrease the amount of blood shunted from the right ventricle to the left ventricle, which can improve oxygenation in children with tetralogy of Fallot. In contrast, supine and prone positions can worsen cyanosis and dyspnea, and leaning forward can help but is not as effective as squatting.",
