                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking about a trend in the increase of non-communicable disease cases compared to previous years.\n\nStep 2: Define the options\nA) Seasonal - refers to changes that occur in a regular pattern throughout the year.\nB) Cyclical - refers to changes that occur in a regular pattern over a longer period of time.\nC) Periodical - refers to changes that occur in a regular pattern over a specific period of time.\nD) Secular - refers to changes that occur over a long period of time, usually decades or centuries.\n\nStep 3: Eliminate options\nOption A can be eliminated because non-communicable diseases are not typically affected by seasonal changes. Option B can also be eliminated because the trend is not occurring in a regular pattern over a longer period of time. Option C can be eliminated because the trend is not occurring in a regular pattern over a specific period of time.\n\nStep 4: Choose the correct answer\nThe correct answer is D) Secular, as the trend of increasing non-communicable disease cases is occurring over a long period of time, usually decades or centuries.",
