                        "cot": " Epistaxis is bleeding from the nose. To control epistaxis, we need to stop the bleeding. To stop the bleeding, we need to tie off the vessel that is bleeding.\n\nThe maxillary artery is a branch of the external carotid artery. The anterior ethmoidal artery is a branch of the internal carotid artery. The internal carotid artery and the external carotid artery are the two main arteries that supply blood to the head and neck.\n\nSo, we can see that the internal carotid artery and the external carotid artery are the two vessels that need to be ligated in order to control epistaxis. The answer is C) Internal carotid artery and D) External carotid artery.",
