                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nC) Longitudinal study. This design would allow for the collection of data over time from both pre-term and term infants, allowing for comparisons to be made between the two groups. A case control study would only compare the fat content in breast milk from pre-term and term infants at a single point in time, while a prospective cohort study would only follow one group of infants (either pre-term or term) over time. Ambispective is not a recognized study design.",
                        "answers": [
