                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-03",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "it is important to note that the study design should be chosen based on the research question and objectives, as well as the available resources and feasibility. \n\nIn this case, the research question is comparing the fat content in the expressed breast milk of pre-term infants versus term infants. Therefore, a longitudinal study design would be best suited as it allows for the collection of data over time and can track changes in the fat content of breast milk in both groups of infants. \n\nA case-control study design would not be appropriate as it is typically used to investigate the association between an exposure and an outcome, and in this case, there is no specific exposure being investigated. \n\nA prospective cohort study design could also be used, but it may be more difficult to recruit and follow pre-term infants over time. \n\nAn ambispective study design is not a commonly used term in research and may not be appropriate for this study.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "d3f61460-695c-403b-b15f-4b19e60d5b03",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
