                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe best way for the person to save money for a nice vacation at the end of the year can be determined through the following steps:\n\nStep 1: Identify the goal\nThe person's goal is to save money for a nice vacation at the end of the year.\n\nStep 2: Analyze the budget and expenses\nThe person needs to analyze their budget and expenses to identify areas where they can cut back on spending and save money.\n\nStep 3: Evaluate the options\nThe options presented are:\nA) make more phone calls\nB) quit eating lunch out\nC) buy less with monopoly money\nD) have lunch with friends\n\nOption A, making more phone calls, is not a viable option for saving money for a vacation as it does not directly impact the person's expenses.\n\nOption B, quitting eating lunch out, is a good option as it can save the person a significant amount of money over time. Eating out can be expensive, and bringing lunch from home can be a more cost-effective option.\n\nOption C, buying less with monopoly money, is not a realistic option as monopoly money is not real money and cannot be used to purchase goods or services.\n\nOption D, having lunch with friends, is not a good option as it can lead to increased spending on food and drinks.\n\nStep 4: Choose the best option\nBased on the analysis, the best option for the person to save money for a nice vacation at the end of the year is to quit eating lunch out and bring lunch from home instead. This can help the person save a significant amount of money over time, which can be put towards their vacation fund.",
