                    {
                        "id": "9fe2f4a4-30d8-447f-959e-477214be4c21",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the basics of eye color inheritance\nEye color is determined by the amount and type of pigments in the iris of the eye. The two main pigments are melanin (brown) and lipochrome (yellow). The amount and combination of these pigments are determined by genes inherited from parents.\n\nStep 2: Look at the eye color of the parents\nThe best way to guess a baby's eye color is to look at the eye color of the parents. This is because eye color is a hereditary trait, and the baby's eye color will depend on the combination of genes inherited from the parents. If both parents have brown eyes, it is likely that the baby will also have brown eyes. If one parent has blue eyes and the other has brown eyes, the baby may have either blue or brown eyes, depending on the specific genes inherited.\n\nStep 3: Consider the eye color of other family members\nIf the eye color of the parents is not a clear indicator, it may be helpful to look at the eye color of other family members, such as grandparents, aunts, uncles, and cousins. This can give a better idea of the possible combinations of genes that the baby may inherit.\n\nStep 4: Understand that eye color can change\nIt is important to note that a baby's eye color can change during the first year of life. This is because the amount and type of pigments in the iris can continue to develop and change during this time. However, once a baby's eye color has stabilized, it is unlikely to change again.\n\nIn conclusion, the best way to guess a baby's eye color is to look at the eye color of the parents and other family members. While there is no guarantee that the baby will have the same eye color as the parents, this is the most reliable method based on the principles of heredity.",
                        "answers": [
