                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe correct answer is D) The Sun.\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- Seasons refer to the changes in weather patterns and temperature that occur in a cyclic manner throughout the year.\n- These changes are caused by the varying amount of sunlight that different parts of the Earth receive as it orbits around the Sun.\n- The Earth rotates on its axis, which is an imaginary line passing through its center, once every 24 hours. This rotation causes day and night.\n- However, the axis of the Earth is tilted at an angle of about 23.5 degrees relative to its orbit around the Sun.\n- This means that as the Earth orbits the Sun, different parts of it receive varying amounts of sunlight depending on their position relative to the Sun.\n- When the Northern Hemisphere is tilted towards the Sun, it receives more direct sunlight and experiences summer, while the Southern Hemisphere is tilted away and experiences winter.\n- Six months later, when the Earth has completed half of its orbit, the situation is reversed, and the Northern Hemisphere experiences winter while the Southern Hemisphere experiences summer.\n- Therefore, it is the Sun's position relative to the Earth's tilted axis that causes the seasons, not the rotation of the Earth itself, the atmosphere, or the equator.",
