                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\n1. The plant is perennial, meaning it lives for more than one growing season.\n2. It has an elongated stem, which suggests it is a tree or a tall shrub.\n3. It is frequently used for lumber, which means it is a valuable source of wood.\n4. The question asks why it would fall to the ground.\n\nA) It's dead - This is a possibility, but the question doesn't give any indication that the plant is dead. It only says that it is frequently used for lumber, which suggests it is alive and healthy.\n\nB) For water - This doesn't make sense. Trees and tall shrubs have deep roots that can access water underground, so they don't need to fall to the ground to get water.\n\nC) For food - This also doesn't make sense. Plants make their own food through photosynthesis, so they don't need to fall to the ground to get nutrients.\n\nD) For sun - This is the most likely answer. If the plant is tall and has an elongated stem, it may be top-heavy and prone to falling over in high winds or heavy rain. Falling to the ground would allow it to access more sunlight and continue growing, even if it is no longer upright. Additionally, if the plant is old or diseased, it may be more likely to fall over due to weakened roots or stem.",
