                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we need to understand when humans evolved. According to scientific evidence, the earliest known human-like species, Homo habilis, lived around 2.8 million years ago. \n\nNext, we need to know when fossil fuels were formed. Fossil fuels, such as coal, oil, and natural gas, are formed from the remains of dead plants and animals that lived millions of years ago. These remains were buried under sediment and rock, and over time, heat and pressure transformed them into fossil fuels. \n\nBased on this information, we can conclude that humans predate fossil fuel formation. Therefore, the correct answer is B) humans predate fossil fuel formation.",
