                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nB) humans predate fossil fuel formation.\n\nThe formation of fossil fuels, such as coal, oil, and natural gas, requires millions of years of geological processes. These processes involve the decomposition and compression of organic matter, such as plants and animals, over long periods of time. \n\nHumans, on the other hand, evolved relatively recently in geological terms, with the earliest known human species, Homo habilis, appearing around 2.8 million years ago. This means that humans predate the formation of fossil fuels, and therefore, option B is the correct answer. \n\nOption A is incorrect because fossil fuels were not created by humans, but rather, they are a natural resource that humans have discovered and extracted from the earth. Option C is also incorrect because while significant supplies of fossil fuels have accumulated over time, this accumulation occurred after humans had already evolved. Option D is incorrect because option B is the correct answer.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "a45ffb0c-9e12-4193-a8fb-e405443c3779",
