                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understanding the question\nThe question is asking which organ is the most muscular among the given options.\n\nStep 2: Analyzing the options\nA) Lungs: Lungs are not muscular organs. They are made up of spongy tissue and do not have any muscles.\nB) Kidney: Kidneys are not muscular organs. They are made up of specialized cells that filter blood and remove waste products.\nC) Heart: The heart is a muscular organ that pumps blood throughout the body. It is made up of cardiac muscle tissue, which is a specialized type of muscle that contracts involuntarily.\nD) Liver: The liver is not a muscular organ. It is a large, complex organ that performs many vital functions, including filtering blood, producing bile, and storing nutrients.\n\nStep 3: Conclusion\nBased on the analysis, the most muscular organ among the given options is the heart (option C).",
