                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, a flower needs to attract pollinators such as bees, butterflies, and birds. This is usually done through bright colors, sweet fragrances, and nectar. \n\nOnce a pollinator lands on the flower, it collects pollen from the flower's male reproductive organs (stamens) and transfers it to the female reproductive organs (pistils) of another flower of the same species. This process is called pollination. \n\nThe ultimate goal of a flower is to be successfully fertilized, which means that the pollen from the male reproductive organs has successfully reached and fertilized the female reproductive organs. This results in the production of seeds, which will eventually grow into new plants. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) be successfully fertilized.",
