                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the question\nThe question is asking why Bill planted rapeseed in his field one year and soybeans the next.\n\nStep 2: Analyze the options\nA) get bigger yields - This option suggests that Bill planted different crops to get bigger yields. This could be a possibility as different crops have different yields, but we cannot be sure if this was the reason without more information.\nB) make things boring - This option does not make sense as planting different crops would not make things boring.\nC) keep things random - This option suggests that Bill planted different crops to keep things random. This could be a possibility as planting the same crop every year could lead to soil depletion and pest problems. Planting different crops can help break the cycle and keep things random.\nD) get smaller yields - This option does not make sense as no farmer would intentionally plant a crop to get smaller yields.\n\nStep 3: Choose the correct answer\nBased on the analysis, the most likely reason why Bill planted rapeseed in his field one year and soybeans the next is to keep things random. Therefore, the correct answer is C) keep things random.",
