                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "it is important to note that the term \"rapeseed\" is no longer commonly used in agriculture due to its negative connotations. The crop is now referred to as canola. \n\nTo answer the question, the correct answer is A) get bigger yields. Planting different crops in alternating years is a common practice in agriculture known as crop rotation. This helps to improve soil health, reduce pest and disease pressure, and increase yields. Canola and soybeans are both high-yielding crops, so alternating between them can help to maximize production.",
