                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we need to understand that frogs are cold-blooded animals, which means they cannot regulate their body temperature internally like humans do. Instead, they rely on external sources of heat to warm up.\n\nOption A, wearing a Christmas sweater, is not a viable solution for frogs as they do not have the ability to put on clothes.\n\nOption B, drinking hot chocolate, is also not possible for frogs as they do not have the ability to drink or consume food in the same way humans do.\n\nOption C, going for a run, may help frogs generate some heat through physical activity, but it is not a reliable or practical solution for them.\n\nOption D, sitting under a lamp, is the most feasible solution for frogs to get warm. By basking in the light and heat of a lamp, they can raise their body temperature and regulate their metabolism. This is a common behavior observed in many species of frogs and reptiles.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "eb320662-f05d-49b6-9927-2be27c908c4d",
