                        "cot": " \n\nFirst, what does it mean for a frog to be warm? \n\nA frog is warm when its body temperature is warm. \n\nThere are a few ways to warm up a frog's body temperature. \n\nOne way to do this is to wear a Christmas sweater. The sweater will keep the frog's body warm. \n\nAnother way to do this is to drink a hot chocolate. The hot chocolate will raise the frog's body temperature. \n\nA third way to do this is to go for a run. The frog's body will generate heat as it runs, and this will raise its body temperature. \n\nA fourth way to do this is to sit under a lamp. The lamp will provide warmth to the frog's body, and this will raise its body temperature.",
