                        "cot": "A) Regurgitation - This is the process of bringing swallowed food back up into the mouth, which is not what worms do with dead organisms.\nB) Decomposition - This is the process of breaking down organic matter into simpler compounds, which is what worms contribute to when they consume dead organisms and release nutrients back into the soil.\nC) Recycling - This is a more general term for reusing materials, but it doesn't specifically describe what worms do with dead organisms.\nD) Burial - This refers to placing something in the ground, which is not the main action worms perform when consuming dead organisms.\n\nBased on these definitions, the best answer is:\n\nB) Decomposition",
