                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nC) daughter\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n1. Punnett square is a tool used to predict the probability of offspring inheriting certain traits from their parents.\n\n2. The Punnett square is based on the principles of Mendelian genetics, which states that each individual has two copies of each gene, one from each parent.\n\n3. The Punnett square is a grid that shows all possible combinations of alleles (different forms of a gene) that can occur when gametes (sperm and egg cells) combine during fertilization.\n\n4. The Punnett square can be used to calculate the chance of a trait being passed to someone's daughter because the daughter inherits one copy of each gene from her father and one copy from her mother.\n\n5. For example, if we want to know the probability of a daughter inheriting a dominant trait (represented by the letter \"A\") from her heterozygous father (who has one dominant \"A\" allele and one recessive \"a\" allele) and a homozygous recessive mother (who has two recessive \"a\" alleles), we can use a Punnett square.\n\n6. The Punnett square for this cross would look like this:\n\n|   | A | a |\n|---|---|---|\n| a | Aa| aa|\n| a | Aa| aa|\n\n7. The four boxes in the Punnett square represent the possible combinations of alleles that can occur when the father's sperm and the mother's egg combine.\n\n8. The probability of the daughter inheriting the dominant \"A\" allele from her father is 50%, because there are two possible outcomes that result in the daughter having at least one \"A\" allele (Aa and AA), out of a total of four possible outcomes.\n\n9. Therefore, the Punnett square can be used to calculate the chance of a trait being passed to someone's daughter.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "b7ba7cbf-4acf-4da2-ab7f-42437b464c26",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
