                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we need to understand why we need a reflector when running at night. The answer is simple: to make ourselves visible to drivers and other pedestrians. \n\nNow, let's look at the options:\n\nA) A black shirt: This is not a good option as black absorbs light and makes us less visible.\n\nB) Kitchen foil: This could work in a pinch, but it may not be very durable or comfortable to wear.\n\nC) Sunglasses: This is not a good option as sunglasses are designed to reduce glare, not reflect light.\n\nD) A megaphone: This is not a good option as a megaphone is not designed to be worn and would not reflect light.\n\nSo, the best answer is B) Kitchen foil, but a better option would be to invest in a reflective vest or tape specifically designed for running at night.",
