                    },
                    {
                        "id": "7eba54af-851a-4a77-bc93-3a171bb4d5aa",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we need to understand what \"dissolve\" means. When a solid dissolves in a liquid, it means that the solid particles break down and mix evenly with the liquid particles, creating a homogeneous solution.\n\nNow, the temperature of the liquid can affect how well a solid dissolves. Generally, higher temperatures increase the rate of dissolution because the particles move faster and collide more frequently, breaking down the solid more quickly.\n\nTherefore, the best beverage to dissolve solids would be B) A boiling hot mug of tea. The high temperature of the tea would accelerate the dissolution process and help break down the solid particles more effectively. However, it's important to note that not all solids dissolve in all liquids, so the type of solid and the type of beverage also play a role in the dissolution process.",
                        "answers": [
