                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Define instinctual behavior\nInstinctual behavior is a behavior that is innate and automatic, meaning it is not learned or taught.\n\nStep 2: Evaluate each option\nA) Dogs rolling over on command - This is a learned behavior, not instinctual.\nB) Frogs returning to the ponds were they hatched to lay eggs - This is an instinctual behavior as it is innate and automatic.\nC) Birds mimicking human speech - This is a learned behavior, not instinctual.\nD) Seals clapping for treats from trainers - This is a learned behavior, not instinctual.\n\nStep 3: Choose the correct answer\nThe only option that fits the definition of instinctual behavior is B) Frogs returning to the ponds were they hatched to lay eggs. Therefore, the correct answer is B.",
