                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nFirst, we need to identify what an instinctual behavior is. Instinctual behaviors are unlearned, fixed patterns of behavior that are exhibited by all members of a species. \n\nNow that we know what an instinctual behavior is, we can look at our options and see which one is the best fit. \n\nOption A, dogs rolling over on command, is not an instinctual behavior. This is a learned behavior that has been taught to dogs by their owners. \n\nOption B, frogs returning to the ponds were they hatched to lay eggs, is an instinctual behavior. This is a fixed pattern of behavior exhibited by all members of the species. \n\nOption C, birds mimicking human speech, is not an instinctual behavior. This is a learned behavior that has been taught to birds by their owners. \n\nOption D, seals clapping for treats from trainers, is not an instinctual behavior. This is a learned behavior that has been taught to seals by their trainers.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "004b42da-4314-403d-bb84-5f866ddb4190",
