                        "instruction": "qa-01",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nTo determine which of the given options is an instinctual behavior, we need to understand what instinctual behavior means. \n\nInstinctual behavior refers to a behavior that is innate and automatic, meaning it is not learned or taught but rather inherited genetically. It is a behavior that an animal is born with and performs without any prior experience or training. \n\nNow, let's examine each option given in the question to determine which one is an instinctual behavior:\n\nA) Dogs rolling over on command: This behavior is not instinctual because it is learned through training. Dogs do not naturally roll over on command; they are taught to do so by their owners.\n\nB) Frogs returning to the ponds where they hatched to lay eggs: This behavior is instinctual because it is a natural behavior that is genetically programmed into the frog. Frogs instinctively return to the place where they were born to lay their eggs.\n\nC) Birds mimicking human speech: This behavior is not instinctual because it is learned. Birds do not naturally mimic human speech; they learn to do so by hearing and imitating the sounds they hear around them.\n\nD) Seals clapping for treats from trainers: This behavior is not instinctual because it is learned through training. Seals do not naturally clap their flippers to receive treats; they are taught to do so by their trainers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) Frogs returning to the ponds where they hatched to lay eggs, as it is an instinctual behavior.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "c67c33cb-d3a8-4e5f-ae30-875a0e20cfe6",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "B) frogs returning to the ponds where they hatched to lay eggs.",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
