                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nAn instinctual behavior is a behavior that is innate and not learned. It is something that an animal does naturally without being taught. \n\nOption B is the correct answer because it describes a behavior that is innate to the frog species. Frogs have an instinctual drive to return to the same pond where they were born to lay their eggs. This behavior is not learned, but rather programmed into their genetic makeup. \n\nOption A describes a behavior that is learned through training. Dogs do not naturally roll over on command, but can be taught to do so through positive reinforcement training. \n\nOption C describes a behavior that is learned through mimicry. Birds do not naturally mimic human speech, but can learn to do so through exposure to human language. \n\nOption D describes a behavior that is learned through conditioning. Seals do not naturally clap for treats, but can be trained to do so through operant conditioning. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) frogs returning to the ponds were they hatched to lay eggs.",
